# =============================================================================
# Chiron frontend — environment configuration
# Copy to .env (same directory) and fill in real values. Do NOT commit .env.
# =============================================================================
#
# CONVENTIONS
#   - Every frontend variable has the CHIRON_ prefix, grouped by target:
#       CHIRON_MNEMOSYNE_*   Mnemosyne (Rust/Actix)
#       CHIRON_KS_*          Knowledge Store (Python/Flask)
#       CHIRON_*             general interface settings
#   - This convention applies ONLY to the frontend. The Mnemosyne / KS .env files
#     keep their existing variable names (they run in production; not renamed).
#
# WHICH VARIABLES REACH THE BROWSER?
#   Only the variables marked [public] below are embedded in code that runs in
#   the browser (a fixed list in vite.config.ts, not decided by prefix).
#   [server] variables are read only by the Vite dev/preview server — the proxy
#   attaches them to server-side requests, so secrets never appear in DevTools or
#   in the build bundle. Consequence: the frontend must be run with `npm run dev`
#   or `npm run preview`; opening the static files in dist/ directly leaves
#   Knowledge and Note scan without a proxy to call.
#
# MAPPING TO MODULE VARIABLES (for reference; the frontend does NOT read these)
#   CHIRON_MNEMOSYNE_URL   ↔ Mnemosyne binds 127.0.0.1:8081 (main.rs)
#   CHIRON_KS_URL          ↔ KS_HTTP_PORT            (knowledgeStore/.env)
#   CHIRON_KS_TOKEN        ↔ KS_HTTP_TOKEN           (knowledgeStore/.env, Mnemosyne/.env)
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY / LLM_PROVIDER / KS_LLM_* — there is NO CHIRON_ version: the
#     frontend never calls an LLM. Every LLM call goes through Mnemosyne, and the
#     key lives in its .env. Putting an LLM key here only adds a place to leak it.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mnemosyne — studying (Socratic), flashcards, quizzes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [public] The browser calls it DIRECTLY (cross-origin). Mnemosyne only allows
# CORS from http://localhost:5173 / :4173 (and the matching 127.0.0.1) — the
# frontend always runs on these two ports (strictPort). 127.0.0.1 rather than
# localhost because Mnemosyne binds IPv4 only.
CHIRON_MNEMOSYNE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081

# There is deliberately NO Mnemosyne token variable here: the learner's token
# lives in the browser (pasted on the Settings screen), like any web sign-in.
# Putting it in .env would only create another copy of the secret. Issue one with:
#   cd mnemosyne && cargo run -p backend -- create-user <email>


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Knowledge Store — the "Knowledge" area
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [server] KS address. The browser does NOT call it directly: it calls /api/ks/*
# on the Vite server, and the proxy forwards here (GET /health, /nodes,
# /nodes/{id} and the Note scan routes — a fixed list in server/chironProxy.ts).
# KS runs on port 8080 by default (KS_HTTP_PORT); if 8080 is taken on your
# machine, change KS_HTTP_PORT on the KS side and match the port here.
CHIRON_KS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# [server] SECRET. Must equal KS's KS_HTTP_TOKEN. The proxy sends it as the
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. ASCII only (KS rejects anything else).
# Generate one: openssl rand -hex 32
CHIRON_KS_TOKEN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# General
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [public] Time zone used to display times on every screen.
CHIRON_TIMEZONE=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh
